tial race as a genuine tossup. The state has trended toward Republicans in recent cycles, and with a term-limited president leaving the ballot open, neither party starts with an incumbency advantage. No public polls, expert ratings, or fundraising figures are yet available for the general election, so the outlook rests on the state's fundamental partisan lean, which favors Republicans by about a point.\n\nThat edge is small enough to sit well within the range of normal variation. Nevada's electorate, shaped by a large Latino and union-household vote and heavy early voting, has decided recent presidential contests by razor-thin margins, and both parties' nominating fights are giving the state early attention. The race projects as close with a slight Republican tilt, and uncertainty should stay wide until real polling arrives.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4561, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4622, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4656, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4628, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4646, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4672, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4612, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4728, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4601, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4654, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4647, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4638, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.469, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.4636, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.46, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.4592, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.4612, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.463, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.4555, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.4656, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "202